// ============================================================================
// 06 - WordPress admin/content activity + writes in a window
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Purpose : the targeted drill-down. Combines the two things worth watching on
//           a WordPress-shaped app: touches on /wp-admin/ and /wp-content/,
//           plus every write attempt regardless of path. One OR'd filter so a
//           single pass shows both the recon and the action.
// Use it  : the "what did they actually do" query. Run it on the window that
//           queries 01/02 pointed you at, then widen the window to follow the
//           session forward in time.
// Table   : AppServiceHTTPLogs
//
// TUNABLES:
//   datetime window        -> START narrow (15 min), then widen (1h, 6h) to
//                             follow the session. This is the main knob.
//   contains "/wp-admin/"  -> for non-WordPress apps swap for your own
//                             sensitive prefixes: "/admin/", "/api/",
//                             "/actuator/", "/.env", "/.git/", "/phpmyadmin/"
//   CsMethod in ("POST","PUT") -> see query 03 notes
//   add `| where CIp in ("x.x.x.x", "y.y.y.y")` -> pin to known-bad IPs
//   add UserAgent to project   -> spot tooling (curl, python-requests, sqlmap)
//
// NOTE: mind operator precedence. KQL evaluates `and` before `or`, so if you
//       add an IP restriction to this line rather than a separate `| where`,
//       parenthesise the OR group or the filter will not do what you expect.
// ============================================================================
AppServiceHTTPLogs
| where TimeGenerated between (datetime(2026-09-02 02:15) .. datetime(2026-09-02 03:30))
| where CsUriStem contains "/wp-admin/" or CsUriStem contains "/wp-content/" or CsMethod in ("POST","PUT")
| project TimeGenerated, CIp, CsMethod, CsUriStem, CsUriQuery, ScStatus, CsBytes
| sort by TimeGenerated asc
